  "id": "growth-spurt",
  "term": "growth spurt",
  "definition": "A growth spurt, in this context, is a developmental window of especially rapid brain growth. In humans it occurs in the third trimester of pregnancy and involves major brain-building processes such as neuron production, cell movement, and synapse formation, making it a period that is particularly sensitive to harmful influences that can affect later behavior.",
